    <GaugingStation location="Robstone" name="Girvan" number="82001">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station on the River Girvan. Flows affected by abstractions from Loch Bradan.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Low flow control is an informal gravel weir built in 1982, which is subject to re-grading in substantial floods. Flood banks contain all flows (pre-1982, right bank inundated beyond 2.2m). Peak flow ratings from current meter gaugings. Rating for period up to 1982 max gauging 2.2m (about 0.9 QMED); post-1982 max gauging up to 1.9m (about 0.7 QMED), simple extrapolation beyond. Gaugings to 1982 show scatter; may suggest a changing relationship.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station approx. 15m wide.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Runoff diminished by abstractions from Loch Bradan. Additional storage in a few high level lochs.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Upland catchment draining from Carrick Forest. Complex geology: Ordovician/Carboniferous metamorphics and igneous formations; predominantly overlain by superficial deposits, drift and peat also. Mostly hill pasture with some mixed farming in the valley and afforestation in the headwaters; several lochs.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">S</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to near QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Only after June 1982 when an embankment was built to allow for containment of flows above 2.2m." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
